From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:45:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] vlandev, macvlan: delete a stale device before creating
 it

A netifd that exits without bringing its interfaces down, as on a stop
through procd or after a crash, leaves its vlan and macvlan devices in
the kernel. The next netifd creates them with NLM_F_EXCL, which fails
with -EEXIST, so an interface on such a device fails with
DEVICE_CLAIM_FAILED until the device is removed by hand.

Delete the device before creating it, as veth does since commit
df2f5c9 ("veth: delete device before creation to handle stale state").

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
 macvlan.c | 2 ++
 vlandev.c | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/macvlan.c
+++ b/macvlan.c
@@ -91,6 +91,8 @@ macvlan_set_up(struct macvlan_device *mv
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
+	system_macvlan_del(&mvdev->dev);
+
 	ret = system_macvlan_add(&mvdev->dev, mvdev->parent.dev, &mvdev->config);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto release;
--- a/vlandev.c
+++ b/vlandev.c
@@ -180,6 +180,8 @@ vlandev_set_up(struct vlandev_device *mv
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
+	system_vlandev_del(&mvdev->dev);
+
 	ret = system_vlandev_add(&mvdev->dev, mvdev->parent.dev, &mvdev->config);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto release;
